    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "The Toupet fundoplication is a surgical procedure used to treat gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD). It involves wrapping the fundus of the stomach around the back of the esophagus, creating a 270-degree posterior partial wrap. This wrap is designed to enhance the antireflux barrier while maintaining lower esophageal sphincter function.",
