      "C": "A 180-degree anterior wrap is characteristic of the Dor fundoplication, not the Toupet.\nThe Dor fundoplication is an anterior partial wrap often used in anti-reflux surgery.",
      "D": "The Toupet fundoplication is a surgical procedure used to treat gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD). It involves wrapping the fundus of the stomach around the back of the esophagus, creating a 270-degree posterior partial wrap. This wrap is designed to enhance the antireflux barrier while maintaining lower esophageal sphincter function."
