    "explanation": "Normal cecum has a luminal diameter of 7.5-\n8.5cm and becomes at risk at 10cm. Sigmoid\ncolon is the narrowest part and most vulnerable\nto obstruction and also most mobile and\nvulnerable to volvulus.\nSource: Schwartz’s Principles of Surgery 8th ed\np 1015",
