    "explanation": "Zollinger–Ellison syndrome is caused by a non–\nislet cell tumor that produces gastrin and is\nassociated with gastric acid hypersecretion and\npeptic ulcer disease. Tumors are biologically\nmalignant in 60% of cases, and the most\ncommon site involved is the pancreas. Most\ngastrinomas are found in the gastrinoma\ntriangle (Passaro's triangle): this is bound by the\njunction of cystic and common bile ducts,\njunction of the second and third parts of the\nduodenum, and the junction of the neck and\nbody of the pancreas.",
