    "subject": "surgery",
    "originalNumber": 39,
    "stem": "A 61-year-old man with a history of\ngastroesophageal reflux disease and Barrett’s\nesophagus is undergoing a screening endoscopy.\nThe biopsy results show high-grade dysplasia.\nWhat is the recommended treatment approach?\nA Refer the patient to a surgeon for\nesophagectomy.\nB Repeat surveillance endoscopy in 6 months.\nC Repeat surveillance endoscopy in 1 year.\nD No further endoscopy is indicated unless the\npatient becomes symptomatic.\nE Initiate chemotherapy.",
