    "explanation": "Goodsall's rule relates the external opening of an\nanal fistula to its internal opening. It states that\nthe external opening situated below the\ntransverse anal line will open into the anal canal\nin the midline posteriorly. An anterior opening\nis usually associated with a radial tract. Anterior\nfistulas will have a direct track into the anal\ncanal. Posterior fistulas will have a curved track\nwith their internal opening lying in the posterior\nmidline of the anal canal. An exception to the\nrule are anterior fistulas lying more than 3 cm.\nfrom the anus, which may have a curved track\n(similar to posterior fistulas) that opens into the\nposterior midline of the anal canal.",
