    "correctChoice": "E",
    "explanation": "HNPCC is more common than FAP, but is still\nextremely rare (1 to 3%). The genetic defects\nassociated with HNPCC arise from errors in\nmismatch repair. HNPCC is inherited in an\nautosomal dominant pattern and is\ncharacterized by the development of colorectal\ncarcinoma at an early age (average age: 40 to 45\nyears) Cancers appear in the proximal colon\nmore often than in sporadic colorectal cancer\nand have a better prognosis regardless of stage.\nHNPCC also may be associated with extracolonic\nmalignancies, including endometrial, which is\nmost common",
