    "explanation": "Diagnosis: Diastasis recti. This is a separation of\nthe pillars of rectus abdominis muscles, and may\neither be congenital or acquired in aetiology. A\nSpigelian hernia is not located at the midline and\nis not usually mistaken for diastasis recti.",
