    "explanation": "The Amsterdam criteria for clinical diagnosis of\nHNPCC are three affected relatives with\nhistologically verified adenocarcinoma of the\nlarge bowel (one must be a first-degree relative\nof one of the others) in two successive\ngenerations of a family with one patient\ndiagnosed before age 50 years. FAP is not an\nHNPCC related CA Schwartz 10th pg 1207",
