    "explanation": "Answer: D. Pneumothorax\nNotes: Pneumothorax can inadvertently occur\nwhile introducing a subclavian venous catheter.\nThe patient will complain of sudden dyspnea. A\nchest x-ray film should always be taken after\nsubclavian catheter placement, to determine the\nposition of the tip of the catheter and to exclude\nthe possibility of pneumothorax.",
