    "id": "superexam-surgery-0690",
    "subject": "surgery",
    "originalNumber": 690,
    "stem": "Ten years ago, a 79 yo female with a 25-year\nhistory of type 2 diabetes was diagnosed with\ndiabetic nephropathy. At this time, she is\noverweight but not obese and she smokes about\nthree packs of cigarettes per week. Despite being\ndiagnosed with diabetic nephropathy, she had not\nstopped smoking and in general had not tightly\ncontrolled her blood glucose levels; consequently,\nher renal function has steadily deteriorated and\nher physician now believes she has ESRD. He\narranges for her to undergo hemodialysis. Before\nundergoing hemodialysis, it was also\nrecommended that she have an operation. Which\nof the following choices describes the surgical\nprocedure most likely recommended?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "A renal biopsy"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Insertion of a special, soft catheter through a\nsmall slit made adjacent to the navel under local\nanesthesia"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Performing open surgery and inserting a\ncatheter under general anesthetic"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Formation of an arteriovenous (AV) fistula"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Answer: D. Formation of an arteriovenous\n(AV) fistula\nNotes: To perform hemodialysis, it is necessary\nto surgically form an arteriovenous (AV) fistula.\nThis is accomplished by creating an opening in\nwhich the artery is sewn on to a vein; this is\nusually done in the arm. In hemodialysis, blood\nis withdrawn from an artery and returned via a\nvein.",
