    "subject": "surgery",
    "originalNumber": 691,
    "stem": "A 65 yr-old man w/ a history of chronic alcohol\nabuse has been experiencing epigastric &\nperiumbilical pain asso. w/ nonbilious vomiting\nfor 1 day. He denies any melena or hematemesis.\nIn the past he has had several episodes of similar\npain that sometimes radiated to the back and was\nhospitalized for several days 2 months prior. No\nprevious surgery or medical problems.P/E: BP\n120/80, HR 110 bpm, dry mucous membranes.\nAbdomen not distended, no surgical scars.\nDiminished bowel sounds. Soft abdomen, exhibits\nvoluntary guarding of epigastrium. Serum amylase\nlevel is 550 units/100 ml. What is the most\nreasonable initial step in management of this\npatient?",
